{
  "A short text, count or dot, shown inline or on the corner of a button, avatar or icon. A count above its maximum displays as “99+”, and a count of zero is hidden.": "",
  "Tones and appearance": "",
  "Counts and dots": "Sayılar ve noktalar",
  "Corner placement": "",
  "`position` places the badge on a corner of its container. `Badge.attach` does the same programmatically on any component.": "",
  "A badge is read in place, as part of its container.": "",
  "With a label, the badge is an image with that name (`role=\"img\"`), so a count can describe what it counts.": "",
  "Without a label, a dot is hidden from screen readers (`aria-hidden`). Give it a label when it conveys information.": "",
  "Do not rely on tone alone to convey meaning. Pair it with text or a label.": "",
  "A count is formatted in the kit language (`uiLocale`) and updates when the language changes: “1,234” in English and “1.234” in Turkish.": "",
  "The badge. `data-tone`, `data-variant`, `data-size`, `data-position`, `data-dot`, `data-empty`.": "Badge. `data-tone`, `data-variant`, `data-size`, `data-position`, `data-dot`, `data-empty`.",
  "The element a corner badge is attached to (`position: relative`).": "",
  "Unit: the badge at rest (solid, standard), in each appearance and tone (`accent` … `danger`, `subtle-*`, `outline-*`) and as a `dot`.": "",
  "The badge and the dot, per size.": "",
  "The offset of a corner badge from the corner.": "",
  "The default tone and appearance.": "",
  "Short text, shown when there is no `count`.": "",
  "A count formatted in the kit language. Above `max`, it shows `max+`.": "",
  "The highest count shown in full.": "",
  "Shows a count of 0. Without it, the badge hides at 0.": "",
  "Shows a dot only, indicating that something is present.": "",
  "`standard`, `accent`, `info`, `success`, `caution` or `danger`. Material uses `danger` for counts, and the other design languages use `accent`.": "",
  "Set by the design language (`solid`)": "",
  "`top-end`, `top-start`, `bottom-end` or `bottom-start`: the corner of the container, which becomes its anchor. `start` and `end` follow the writing direction.": "",
  "The text announced by screen readers (“3 unread messages”). Without it, they read the badge text.": "",
  "The current display text: the formatted count (`99+`), otherwise the text, or `''` for a dot.": "",
  "Places a badge on a corner of a component (`top-end` unless `props` specifies otherwise). The badge becomes a child of the component and is disposed with it.": ""
